      "slug": "ayran-term",
      "term": "Ayran",
      "definition": "A cold salted yoghurt drink served throughout Turkey, drunk alongside spiced meat dishes to balance the heat."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 2 and takes 5 minutes to prepare with no cooking needed. Plain yoghurt and cold milk are blended with salt and a few mint leaves until smooth and slightly frothy. The result is a cool, refreshing drink that is drunk constantly across Turkey, particularly alongside grilled meats and spiced dishes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: salt is not optional here; it is what makes ayran taste like itself rather than a plain yoghurt smoothie. Add it gradually and taste as you go. The drink should be distinctly but pleasantly salty."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-yoghurt",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "whole-milk",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "mint",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "leaves",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-pepper",
              "amount": null,
              "unit": "pinch",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put the yoghurt, cold milk, mint leaves and half a teaspoon of fine salt into the blender."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend on high for 30 seconds until completely smooth and lightly frothy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Taste and adjust the salt. The drink should taste clearly savoury. Add a little more cold water or milk if you prefer a thinner consistency."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour into tall glasses over ice. Add a mint leaf to each glass and a pinch of black pepper if you like. Drink immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Drink tastes bland"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This is almost always a salt issue. Ayran needs more salt than you might expect. Add another pinch, blend briefly and taste again. Without enough salt it tastes like watered-down yoghurt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Froth disappears quickly"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend for the full 30 seconds and serve immediately. The froth is a natural result of aerating the yoghurt and dissipates within a few minutes. Commercial ayran uses special equipment to hold the foam; home versions are naturally shorter-lived."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Drink is too thick"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turkish ayran is typically quite thin, closer to a drink than a smoothie. Add cold water a tablespoon at a time, blending briefly between additions, until you reach the consistency you want."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cold and salted, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ayran-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ayran"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the national drink of Turkey in all but name, outselling cola in many parts of the country. It is drunk at breakfast, alongside grilled meats, with kofte and at roadside stops. The combination of yoghurt and salt cools the body and cuts through the richness of spiced lamb far more effectively than any soft drink. Made fresh and served immediately over ice, it is hard to beat on a warm day."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}